  "self_load_only": true,
  "description": "bigville R69 (block 385000): WORLD ACTIONS ARE A DATA STRUCTURE, NOT CODE. An ActionSpec is a recipe data row -- name, requires (role), two typed inputs (kind+qty), an output (kind+qty), difficulty, time_minutes, wear_rate. ONE generic rule (ax_do) executes ANY recipe: it names no action, reads everything from the data, consumes the inputs from stock, produces the output, and tires the actor by the difficulty. Adding a new action -- saw planks, tan leather, grind flour -- is a DATA ROW, no code. This is the unifying model the bespoke craft rules (cc_burn, cr_forge_simple, ...) collapse into. Items are likewise data (Stock{kind,qty}; discrete tools carry per-unit props via ToolSpec). Deferred: N-ary recipes (more input slots or ingredient iteration); discrete per-item outputs with individual wear; folding time via the worktime engine.",
