  "rules": [
    {
      "name": "ax_do",
      "batch": false,
      "comment": "GENERIC RECIPE ENGINE -- actions are DATA, not code. An actor 'doing' an ActionSpec whose requires-role he has, and whose two input Stocks (matched by kind) hold enough, executes the recipe: input1 -= in1_qty, input2 -= in2_qty, output += out_qty, and the actor's fatigue += the recipe's difficulty. Unused input slots use the 'none' stock (in2_kind='none', qty 0). This ONE rule runs burn-charcoal, smelt-iron, forge-nails, saw-planks and any recipe added as a data row -- it names no action. (Time_to_make/wear_rate are carried as data too; the worktime engine consumes time_minutes, and wear_rate applies to the tool used.) (Bulk/material outputs only: out_discrete==0, the default; tool outputs go through ax_forge -> discrete items.)",
